/**
@mainpage Vehicle Maintenance System

@section overview Overview
Vehicle Maintenance System is a C++17 command-line program for storing and
managing vehicles and their maintenance records.

@section capabilities Main capabilities
- Add, list, search, edit, and remove vehicles.
- Record maintenance history and view upcoming maintenance.
- Load and save vehicle and maintenance data using CSV files.
- Validate user input before accepting values.

@section architecture Architecture
- **Vehicle** represents vehicle details, including plate number, model,
  model year, and mileage.
- **MaintenanceRecord** represents maintenance information associated with a vehicle.
- **VehicleManager** manages vehicle records and maintenance operations.
- **MaintenanceSystemFacade** provides the command-line workflow for the application.
- **FileManager** handles CSV persistence.

The application demonstrates the **Facade** design pattern in its console
interface and uses **Singleton** for its file manager.

@section building Building and running
From the project root in MSYS2 UCRT64:
@code{.sh}
./build.sh
./_start.sh
@endcode

@section testing Unit testing
Unit tests use GoogleTest. Run them after building:
@code{.sh}
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
@endcode

@section documentation Generating documentation
Install Doxygen in MSYS2 UCRT64, then run from the project root:
@code{.sh}
doxygen Doxyfile
@endcode
Open `build/docs/html/index.html` in a browser to explore the generated API.

@note Generated documentation is stored under `build/` and is not committed
when the existing `.gitignore` excludes that directory.
*/
